CUTER√çA:Charcuter√≠a refers to cured meats that are often high in purines and can contribute to hyperuricemia.CAZA:CAZA refers to game meat, which is known for its nutritional content, containing 7.7 mg of iron per 100 grams. However, it is important to note that caza, or game meats, are often high in purines, which can lead to increased uric acid levels when consumed.AVES:Aves, or birds, can vary in purine content, but certain types can contribute to elevated uric acid levels.PALOMA:Paloma, or pigeon, is a type of bird that can be high in purines and may affect uric acid levels.EXTRACTOS DE CARNE:Extractos de carne, or meat extracts, are concentrated sources of purines that can elevate uric acid levels.PAVO:Pavo, or turkey, is a type of poultry that can have moderate purine levels, influencing uric acid levels.ANCHOAS:Anchoas, or anchovies, are fish that are high in purines and can lead to increased uric acid levels.ARENQUE:Arenque, or herring, is a fish that is high in purines and can contribute to elevated uric acid levels.BACALAO FRESCO:Bacalao fresco, or fresh cod, is a fish that can vary in purine content and influence uric acid levels.QUESOS MUY FERMENTADOS:Quesos muy fermentados, or highly fermented cheeses, can have varying purine levels that may affect uric acid.CHAMPI√ëONES:Champi√±ones, or mushrooms, can have moderate purine content and may influence uric acid levels.INTEGRALES:Cereales integrales, or whole grains, generally have low purine content and can be part of a diet for managing uric acid.GERMEN Y SALVADO DE TRIGO:Germen y salvado de trigo, or wheat germ and bran, are low in purines and can be included in a diet for uric acid management.RESTO CEREALES:Resto cereales, or other cereals, can vary in purine content and may influence uric acid levels.ZUMOS DE FRUTAS:Zumos de frutas, or fruit juices, can contain fructose, which may influence uric acid levels.)<|COMPLETE|>√ÅCIDO OR√ìTICO:√Åcido or√≥tico is a compound found in milk that may have uricosuric effects, helping to lower uric acid levels.BOIX GC:Boix GC is an author who contributed to the literature on kidney stones, specifically in the publication "Litiasis Renal."L√ìPEZ-TORRES HJ:L√≥pez-Torres HJ is an author who co-wrote about kidney stones in the publication "Litiasis Renal."√ÅLVAREZ DL:√Ålvarez DL is an author involved in the research and publication regarding kidney stones.V√ÅZQUEZ CM:V√°zquez CM is an author who contributed to the study of kidney stones in the publication "Litiasis Renal."ROMERO HE:Romero HE is an author who has researched and published findings on kidney stones.JIM√âNEZ LM:Jim√©nez LM is an author who has contributed to the literature on kidney stones.CRIBADO METAB√ìLICO:Cribado metab√≥lico is a comprehensive metabolic screening process recommended for patients with a history of kidney stones to understand the underlying causes.HIPOCAURIAS:Hipocalciurias refers to low levels of calcium in the urine, which can be a factor in the formation of kidney stones.HIPEROXALURIAS:Hiperoxalurias refers to high levels of oxalate in the urine, which can contribute to the formation of certain types of kidney stones.HIPOCITRATURIAS:Hipocitraturias refers to low levels of citrate in the urine, which can increase the risk of kidney stone formation.ALTERACIONES DEL PH URINARIO:Alteraciones del pH urinario refers to changes in urine pH that can affect the solubility of various substances and contribute to kidney stone formation.RECURRENCIA:Recurrencia refers to the repeated occurrence of kidney stones, which can be influenced by dietary and metabolic factors.SCALES CD JR:Scales CD Jr is an author who contributed to research on the prevalence of kidney stones in the United States.SMITH AC:Smith AC is a co-author of the study on the prevalence of kidney stones in the United States.HANLEY JM:Hanley JM is a co-author of the study on the prevalence of kidney stones in the United States.MORGAN MSC:Morgan MSC is an author who wrote about the medical management of renal stones.PEARLE MS:Pearle MS is a notable figure in the field of urology, recognized for their contributions to the medical management of renal stones. They are a co-author of an article that discusses the medical management of renal stones and have also authored the American Urological Association (AUA) guideline on the medical management of kidney stones. Through these works, Pearle MS has played a significant role in shaping the standards and practices related to kidney stone treatment.GONZ√ÅLEZ G:Gonz√°lez G is a researcher specializing in renal lithiasis, also known as nephrolithiasis, and its endocrinological management. In addition to their research, Gonz√°lez G is an author who has contributed to the field by writing about nephrolithiasis within a clinical nephrology context.WORCESTER EM:Worcester EM is an author who has contributed to the clinical practice guidelines on calcium kidney stones.COE FL:Coe FL is a co-author of the clinical practice guidelines on calcium kidney stones.√ÅLVAREZ-LARIO B:√Ålvarez-Lario B is an author who has discussed hyperuricemia and its dietary implications.ALONSO-VALDIVIELSO JL:Alonso-Valdivielso JL is a co-author discussing hyperuricemia and diet.EMMERSON BT:Emmerson BT is an author who has written about the management of gout.RICHTE P:Richette P is an author who has contributed to the understanding of gout.CHIO HK:Choi HK is a researcher who has studied the relationship between soft drinks, fructose consumption, and gout risk.LANSAPA MA:Lanaspa MA is an author who has researched the biological mechanisms of uric acid and fructose.SUNDSTR√ñM J:Sundstr√∂m J is a researcher who has studied serum uric acid levels and their relation to blood pressure and hypertension.HJORTNAES J:Hjortnaes J is a researcher who has studied serum uric acid levels and vascular diseases.REIR CJ:Reir CJ is an author who has researched serum urate as a predictor of outcomes after acute stroke.PAK CY:Pak CY is an author who has contributed to the classification and evaluation of nephrolithiasis.CALCIUM KIDNEY STONES:Calcium kidney stones are a type of kidney stone that forms when calcium combines with other substances in the urine, often requiring dietary management.CHOI HK:Choi HK is a researcher who studied the independent impact of gout on mortality and coronary heart disease.CURHAN G:Curhan G is a researcher involved in studies related to kidney stones and dietary impacts on health.ZUCKERMAN JM:Zuckerman JM is a researcher who has studied hypocitraturia and its medical management.ELDER JS:Elder JS is an author of a chapter on urinary lithiasis in a pediatric textbook.T√úRK C:T√ºrk C is a contributor to the European Association of Urology Guidelines on Urolithiasis.FINK HA:Fink HA is a researcher who conducted a systematic review on dietary prevention of nephrolithiasis.OTSUKI M:Otsuki M is a researcher who studied the association of urine acidification with obesity and metabolic syndrome.PREZIOSO D:Prezioso D is a researcher reviewing dietary treatments for urinary risk factors for renal stone formation.BORGHI L:Borghi L is a researcher who studied urinary volume and water intake in relation to calcium nephrolithiasis.SWEENEY DD:Sweeney DD is a researcher who studied the effects of sports beverages on urinary stone risk factors.EUROPEAN ASSOCIATION OF UROLOGY:The European Association of Urology provides guidelines and recommendations for urological practices, including urolithiasis management.NELSON TEXTBOOK OF PEDIATRICS:The Nelson Textbook of Pediatrics is a comprehensive medical textbook that includes information on urinary lithiasis.AMERICAN UROLOGICAL ASSOCIATION:The American Urological Association is a professional organization that publishes guidelines for the medical management of kidney stones.URINARY LITHIASIS:Urinary lithiasis is the formation of stones in the urinary tract, a central topic in the referenced studies.CALCIUM NEPHROLITHIASIS:Calcium nephrolithiasis is a specific type of kidney stone disease that is frequently addressed in the literature.LOW-SALT DIET:A low-salt diet is examined for its effects on idiopathic hypercalciuria and calcium-oxalate stone formation.FRANCISCO BOTELLA ROMERO:Francisco Botella Romero is a medical professional specializing in endocrinology and nutrition. He is associated with the Complejo Hospitalario Universitario in Albacete and has made significant contributions to various topics in nutrition pathology.√ÅLVARO GARC√çA-MANZANARES V√ÅZQUEZ:√Ålvaro Garc√≠a-Manzanares V√°zquez is a doctor specializing in endocrinology and nutrition at Hospital General La Mancha Centro in Alc√°zar de San Juan, Ciudad Real.IRENE GONZALO MONTESINOS:Irene Gonzalo Montesinos is a medical professional specializing in endocrinology and nutrition. She is affiliated with Hospital Infanta Elena in Valdemoro, Madrid, as well as with Hospital Universitario Infanta Elena and Fundaci√≥n Jim√©nez D√≠az, both located in Madrid.HOSPITAL GENERAL DE VILLALBA:The Hospital General de Villalba is a medical institution located in Madrid, specializing in endocrinology and nutrition. It is noted for its focus on these areas of healthcare, providing specialized services to patients. Nuria Gil Fournier is one of the professionals working at this hospital, contributing to its mission in the fields of endocrinology and nutrition.HOSPITAL GENERAL LA MANCHA CENTRO:Hospital General La Mancha Centro is a hospital located in Alc√°zar de San Juan, Ciudad Real, specializing in endocrinology and nutrition.HOSPITAL INFANTA ELENA:Hospital Infanta Elena is a hospital located in Valdemoro, Madrid, specializing in endocrinology and nutrition.DIARREA Y ESTRE√ëIMIENTO:Diarrea y estre√±imiento are gastrointestinal symptoms that signify potential underlying structural or functional alterations within the digestive system. These conditions are often discussed in the context of nutrition pathology, highlighting their significance in understanding digestive health. Additionally, the topic of diarrea y estre√±imiento is closely related to the role of probiotics and prebiotics in promoting gut health, suggesting that these beneficial microorganisms may play a crucial role in managing and alleviating these symptoms.UROLOGY:Urology is a peer-reviewed medical journal that focuses on the field of urology and related topics.AMERICAN JOURNAL OF KIDNEY DISEASES:The American Journal of Kidney Diseases is a peer-reviewed journal that focuses on research related to kidney disease and its management.HYPEROXALURIA:Hyperoxaluria is a condition characterized by excessive oxalate in the urine, which can lead to kidney stones and other complications.NUTRITION PATHOLOGY:Nutrition pathology refers to the study of how nutritional factors contribute to disease processes and health outcomes.HUMAN MICROBIOME PROJECT:The Human Microbiome Project is a research initiative launched in 2008, focused on understanding the role of the human microbiome in health and disease. This project aims to characterize the human microbiome through the application of modern genetic techniques, providing insights into how these microbial communities influence various aspects of human health.ACIDO ACETICO:Acido Acetico is a primary substrate for cholesterol synthesis, metabolized in muscle.HOUTHELING Y WALKER:Houghteling and Walker are authors of a significant article published in 2015 discussing immunological mechanisms and their relation to health.BACTERIAS INTESTINALES:Intestinal bacteria play a crucial role in nutrient absorption and immune function.ESTEATOHEPATITIS:Esteatohepatitis is a liver condition that may be related to gut health and the microbiome.ATOPIA:Atopia is an allergic condition that can be influenced by the gut microbiome during early life.ENTEROCOLITIS:Enterocolitis is an inflammatory condition of the intestine that can manifest in infants, especially those with APLV (Allergic Proctocolitis due to Cow's Milk Protein) not mediated by IgE. This condition leads to various digestive issues and is often associated with imbalances in the gut microbiome.COLONOCITO:ELIE METCHNIKOFF:Elie Metchnikoff was a Russian scientist and Nobel laureate known for his research on lactic acid bacteria and their health benefits, particularly in promoting longevity.ALFRED NISSLE:Alfred Nissle was a German professor who isolated a non-pathogenic strain of E. coli from a soldier's feces during World War I, contributing to the understanding of probiotics.ORGANIZACI√ìN MUNDIAL DE GASTROENTEROLOG√çA:The Organizaci√≥n Mundial de Gastroenterolog√≠a (World Gastroenterology Organization) is an influential organization dedicated to advancing gastrointestinal health. It plays a crucial role in setting criteria for probiotics, ensuring that their health benefits are scientifically validated. Additionally, the organization provides comprehensive guidelines and recommendations related to gastrointestinal health, which include the use of both probiotics and prebiotics. Through its efforts, the Organizaci√≥n Mundial de Gastroenterolog√≠a promotes research in the field, contributing to the overall understanding and improvement of gastrointestinal health practices.PROBI√ìTICOS:Probiotics are live microorganisms that confer health benefits to the host, particularly in the realm of gastrointestinal health. These beneficial bacteria have the potential to reduce inflammation and improve health outcomes in various conditions when consumed in adequate amounts. Overall, probiotics play a significant role in promoting health and well-being.DISBIOSIS:DISBIOSIS refers to an imbalance in the gut microbiota, which can lead to various health issues and diseases in both children and adults. Probiotics are often used to correct this imbalance, aiming to improve health outcomes. The condition is associated with a range of diseases, highlighting the importance of maintaining a healthy gut microbiome for overall well-being.SCCHAROMYCES CEREVISIAE:Sccharomyces cerevisiae is a species of yeast used as a probiotic, known for its role in fermentation and health benefits.DIARREA ASOCIADA A ANTIBI√ìTICOS:DIARREA ASOCIADA A ANTIBI√ìTICOS (Antibiotic-Associated Diarrhea) is a condition that probiotics have shown potential benefits in treating.INFECCI√ìN POR CLOSTRIDIUM DIFFICILE:INFECCI√ìN POR CLOSTRIDIUM DIFFICILE (Clostridium difficile infection) is a serious condition that probiotics may help manage, according to research.POUCHITIS:POUCHITIS is an inflammatory condition that can occur after surgery and is being studied for probiotic treatment options.PREB√ìTICOS:Prebiotics are ingredients that resist digestion and stimulate the growth of beneficial bacteria in the gut.DIARREA AGUDA DE ORIGEN VIRAL:DIARREA AGUDA DE ORIGEN VIRAL (Acute Diarrhea of Viral Origin) is a condition that probiotics have shown potential benefits in treating.PA√çSES AFRICANOS:African countries are significantly affected by diarrhea, with a high incidence of cases leading to child mortality.PA√çSES DEL SUDESTE ASI√ÅTICO:Southeast Asian countries experience a high prevalence of diarrhea, particularly among children under five years old.PA√çSES INDUSTRIALIZADOS:The term "PA√çSES INDUSTRIALIZADOS" refers to industrialized countries, which typically do not encounter life-threatening risks from acute diarrhea. However, these countries do experience socio-sanitary impacts associated with chronic diarrhea, which has a higher prevalence in these regions due to various lifestyle factors.LACTULOSA:Lactulosa is a synthetic sugar that serves multiple purposes in health care. Primarily, it is recognized as a laxative used to treat constipation. Additionally, Lactulosa functions as a prebiotic, resisting digestion and promoting gut health. This dual role highlights its importance in both alleviating digestive issues and supporting overall gastrointestinal well-being.INULINA:Inulina is a type of soluble fiber that serves as a prebiotic, promoting the growth of beneficial gut bacteria. It is commonly used in dietary and nutritional products due to its health benefits and positive effects on digestive health. Inulina is recognized for its prebiotic properties, making it a valuable ingredient in various food products aimed at enhancing gut health.FRUCTOLOSGALACTOLIGOSAC√ÅRIDOS:Fructooligosaccharides (FOS) are prebiotic carbohydrates that promote the growth of beneficial bacteria in the gut.S√çNDROME DEL INTESTINO IRRITABLE:El s√≠ndrome del intestino irritable (SIC), conocido en ingl√©s como Irritable Bowel Syndrome (IBS), es una condici√≥n gastrointestinal com√∫n que puede ser influenciada por la dieta y la fermentaci√≥n de alimentos. Esta afecci√≥n se caracteriza por s√≠ntomas como dolor abdominal y cambios en los h√°bitos intestinales, que pueden incluir episodios de diarrea. El s√≠ndrome del intestino irritable es frecuentemente discutido en el contexto de la salud intestinal, lo que resalta su relevancia en el bienestar general del sistema digestivo.GALACTOLOSGALACTOLIGOSAC√ÅRIDOS:DIARREA INVASIVA:Diarrea invasiva or dysentery is a more severe form of diarrhea where mucus or blood is present in the stool, often linked to infections by specific pathogens.ESCHIRICHIA COLI:Escherichia coli is a type of bacteria that can cause severe gastrointestinal illness, including diarrhea.ENTAMOEBA HISTOLYTICA:Entamoeba histolytica is a parasitic protozoan that can cause amoebic dysentery and is associated with diarrhea.VIBRIO CHOLERAE:Vibrio cholerae is a bacterium that causes cholera, leading to severe watery diarrhea and high morbidity and mortality rates.SALMONELLA:Salmonella is a genus of bacteria that can cause foodborne illness, often resulting in diarrhea.CAMPYLOBACTER:Campylobacter is a type of bacteria that can lead to gastrointestinal infections, commonly resulting in diarrhea.GIARDIA:Giardia is a protozoan parasite that can cause gastrointestinal illness, leading to persistent diarrhea.CRYPTOSPORIDIUM:Cryptosporidium is a parasite that can cause gastrointestinal infections, often resulting in diarrhea.ETIOLOG√çA:Etiolog√≠a refers to the study of the causes of diseases, in this context, it relates to the causes of diarrhea.BROTE DE EII:Brote de EII refers to an outbreak of inflammatory bowel disease, which can present with symptoms including diarrhea.SRO:SRO refers to Oral Rehydration Solutions, which are used to prevent dehydration caused by diarrhea.DIARREA AGUDA:DIARREA AGUDA, or acute diarrhea, is a medical condition characterized by the rapid onset of frequent loose or watery stools. This condition can be potentially life-threatening if not managed properly, particularly in vulnerable populations such as children and the elderly. Treatment often involves the use of rehydration solutions to prevent dehydration, and in some cases, antibiotics may be required to address underlying infections.RACECADOTRILO:El racecadotril es un f√°rmaco que se utiliza para tratar la diarrea aguda, actuando como un inhibidor de las encefalocinasas y disminuyendo la secreci√≥n intestinal.INMUNODEPRIMIDO:La inmunodepresi√≥n es una condici√≥n que puede aumentar el riesgo de complicaciones en pacientes con diarrea aguda, como aquellos con VIH o que han recibido trasplantes.DIARREA SANGUINOLENTA:Diarrea sanguinolenta, or bloody diarrhea, is a severe symptom that necessitates immediate medical attention. It may indicate a serious underlying infection. This condition is characterized by the presence of blood in the stool and is considered a significant health concern that requires prompt evaluation and treatment.HIDRATACI√ìN ORAL:La hidrataci√≥n oral es un m√©todo de tratamiento clave en la gesti√≥n de la diarrea aguda, utilizando soluciones de rehidrataci√≥n oral para prevenir la deshidrataci√≥n.SOLUCI√ìN DE REHIDRATACI√ìN ORAL:La soluci√≥n de rehidrataci√≥n oral es un tratamiento utilizado para reponer l√≠quidos y electrolitos en pacientes con diarrea aguda.CULTIVO DE HECES:El cultivo de heces es una prueba diagn√≥stica que puede ser necesaria en casos de diarrea aguda para identificar la causa de la infecci√≥n.TRATAMIENTO SINTOM√ÅTICO:El "TRATAMIENTO SINTOM√ÅTICO" se refiere a las intervenciones m√©dicas dise√±adas para aliviar los s√≠ntomas de la diarrea, tanto en casos cr√≥nicos como agudos, sin abordar la causa subyacente de la afecci√≥n. Este enfoque se centra en proporcionar alivio a los pacientes, mejorando su bienestar temporalmente, mientras que la causa ra√≠z de la diarrea permanece sin tratamiento.LACTOBACILLUS RHAMNOSUS GG:Lactobacillus rhamnosus GG is a probiotic strain that has shown effectiveness in managing acute diarrhea, particularly of viral origin.SACCHAROMYCES BOULARDII:Saccharomyces boulardii is a probiotic yeast recognized for its effectiveness in treating gastrointestinal disorders. It is particularly noted for its role in treating and preventing acute diarrhea, especially in cases associated with antibiotic use. Additionally, Saccharomyces boulardii is utilized to support overall gut health, making it a valuable option for individuals seeking to improve their digestive well-being.PROBIOTICS:Probiotics are live microorganisms that offer various health benefits, particularly in the context of gastrointestinal health. They are often included in enteral nutrition to enhance outcomes in trauma patients and have been studied for their potential role in preventing complications associated with severe pancreatic diseases. Probiotics may also help improve gut health and reduce side effects from treatments such as radiotherapy, as well as assist in managing gastrointestinal disorders like acute diarrhea.

However, the use of probiotics in certain populations, particularly immunocompromised patients, is controversial due to potential risks. Additionally, while probiotics may provide benefits in critical care settings, their use is generally not recommended for most ICU patients due to inconsistent data regarding their efficacy. Overall, probiotics are recognized for their potential health benefits, but caution is advised in specific patient groups.PREBIOTICS:Prebiotics are non-digestible food components that play a crucial role in promoting the growth of beneficial microorganisms in the intestines. They are known to stimulate the growth of beneficial bacteria in the gut, which can potentially aid in the management of various gastrointestinal issues, including diarrhea and inflammatory bowel disease. By fostering a healthy gut microbiome, prebiotics contribute to overall digestive health and may offer therapeutic benefits for individuals suffering from these conditions.LEVOFLOXACINO:Levofloxacino is another quinolone antibiotic that can be used to treat severe cases of diarrhea caused by bacterial infections.AZITROMICINA:Azitromicina is a macrolide antibiotic that may be used in cases of acute diarrhea when bacterial infection is suspected.ERITROMICINA:Eritromicina is a macrolide antibiotic that is utilized to treat various bacterial infections, including those that may lead to acute diarrhea. It is particularly effective in critical care patients and can assist in facilitating the passage of a feeding tube through the digestive system. However, it is important to note that eritromicina should be taken on an empty stomach to enhance its absorption. Additionally, the antibiotic can be associated with the production of diarrhea as a side effect. It is also noteworthy that eritromicina can be degraded in an acidic environment, which may impact its absorption.FECAL MICROBIOTA TRANSPLANTATION:Fecal microbiota transplantation (FMT) is a procedure being researched for the treatment of severe and recurrent diarrhea caused by Clostridium difficile.QUINOLONES:PA√çSES EN V√çAS DE DESARROLLO:Developing countries where infectious causes are more prevalent in cases of chronic diarrhea.F75:F75 is a special nutritional treatment formula used for severe acute malnutrition associated with diarrhea in children, administered orally or via a nasogastric tube.F100:F100 is another special nutritional treatment formula for severe acute malnutrition, similar to F75, used in pediatric cases.PL√ÅTANOS:Bananas are recommended for patients with diarrhea due to their potassium content and ability to help firm stools.VEGETALES COCIDOS:Cooked vegetables are advised for patients with diarrhea as they provide essential nutrients while being easier to digest.INTOLERANCIA A LA LACTOSA:Lactose intolerance can develop secondary to infectious enteritis, affecting dietary choices during recovery from diarrhea.ALMID√ìN COCIDO:COLITIS ULCEROSA:Colitis ulcerosa, also known as ulcerative colitis (UC), is an autoimmune disease and a form of inflammatory bowel disease (IBD) that primarily affects the colon and rectum. It is characterized by inflammation and ulceration of the mucosa and submucosa, leading to a range of symptoms including rectal bleeding, abdominal pain, and chronic diarrhea. The condition can result in significant gastrointestinal distress and may lead to nutritional deficits and problems with nutrient absorption, particularly during acute flare-ups. Colitis ulcerosa is a chronic condition that requires ongoing management and may necessitate nutritional intervention to address complications arising from the disease.VASCULITIS:La vasculitis es una inflamaci√≥n de los vasos sangu√≠neos que puede afectar el sistema digestivo y contribuir a la diarrea cr√≥nica.AN√ÅLISIS DE HECES:El an√°lisis de heces es una prueba diagn√≥stica que puede ayudar a identificar la causa de la diarrea cr√≥nica.TRATAMIENTO ETIOL√ìGICO:El tratamiento etiol√≥gico se refiere a las intervenciones m√©dicas que buscan resolver la causa subyacente de la diarrea cr√≥nica.ENFERMEDADES SIST√âMICAS:Las enfermedades sist√©micas son condiciones m√©dicas que pueden afectar m√∫ltiples sistemas del cuerpo y contribuir a s√≠ntomas gastrointestinales.ENFERMEDADES INTESTINALES:Las enfermedades intestinales son trastornos que afectan el intestino y pueden causar s√≠ntomas como diarrea cr√≥nica.ENFERMEDADES DIGESTIVAS NO INTESTINALES:Las enfermedades digestivas no intestinales son condiciones que afectan el sistema digestivo pero no el intestino, y pueden contribuir a la diarrea cr√≥nica.CONSUMO EXCESIVO DE DETERMINADOS INGREDIENTES:El consumo excesivo de ciertos ingredientes puede provocar diarrea cr√≥nica, especialmente en personas sensibles a ellos.ESCHERICHIA COLI NISSLE 1917:Escherichia coli Nissle 1917 is a probiotic strain that has been studied for its beneficial effects in the gastrointestinal tract. It has demonstrated effectiveness in preventing relapses in ulcerative colitis (UC) and may also aid in the treatment of this condition, according to some studies. This specific strain of probiotic bacteria is recognized for its potential therapeutic properties in managing gastrointestinal health, particularly in individuals suffering from ulcerative colitis.VSL#3:VSL#3 is a probiotic formulation that has been studied for its potential benefits in treating ulcerative colitis. It is a specific mixture of probiotics that may also be utilized for the treatment of pouchitis or reservoritis. However, it is important to note that there is a lack of evidence supporting its effectiveness over a placebo in these contexts.CARB√ìN ACTIVADO:Activated carbon is a substance used in medical treatments for its ability to absorb toxins and chemicals.BISMUTO:Bismuth is a chemical element used in some medical treatments, particularly for gastrointestinal issues.RESINAS FIJADORAS DE √ÅCIDOS BILIARES:Bile acid sequestrants are resins used to bind bile acids in the intestine, often used in treating certain gastrointestinal conditions.ALUMINALES:DANE:Diarrea asociada a nutrici√≥n enteral (DANE) refers to diarrhea that is associated with enteral nutrition, which may not always have a clear cause-effect relationship.ZIMMARO:Zimmaro was one of the first researchers to suggest that fiber could prevent diarrhea in patients receiving enteral nutrition.ROMA IV:Los criterios de Roma IV son utilizados para el diagn√≥stico de estre√±imiento funcional, requiriendo la presencia de s√≠ntomas durante al menos 3 meses.CLINDAMICINA:Clindamicina es un antibi√≥tico que puede provocar diarrea en algunos pacientes.CEFALOSPORINAS:Las cefalosporinas son un grupo de antibi√≥ticos que pueden causar diarrea como efecto secundario.COLCHICINA:Colchicina es un f√°rmaco que puede causar diarrea como efecto secundario.CISAPRIDA:Cisaprida is a procin√©tico medication that aids in gastric emptying and stimulates intestinal motility, which can enhance the absorption of enteral nutrition. It is recommended to be taken with meals to minimize gastrointestinal discomfort. However, it is important to note that Cisaprida can be associated with the production of diarrhea. Additionally, the levels of Cisaprida in the body can be increased by the consumption of grapefruit juice, which may affect its efficacy and safety.DOMPERIDONA:Domperidona is a procin√©tico medication that enhances gastric emptying and stimulates intestinal motility. It is recommended to be taken with meals to decrease gastrointestinal discomfort. However, it may also be associated with the production of diarrhea.AINES:Los AINEs (antiinflamatorios no esteroides) pueden causar diarrea como efecto secundario.DIGOXINA:Digoxina es un medicamento utilizado para tratar problemas card√≠acos. Este f√°rmaco puede causar diarrea como efecto secundario. Adem√°s, la bioavailability de la digoxina puede disminuir debido a cambios en la motilidad gastrointestinal provocados por la ingesta de alimentos. Tambi√©n se ha observado que la digoxina puede interactuar con la fibra de la dieta, lo que puede afectar su eficacia.ACARBOSA:Acarbosa es un antidiab√©tico que puede causar diarrea como efecto secundario.5-FLUOROURACILO:5-fluorouracilo, also known as 5-fluorouracil, is an antineoplastic chemotherapy medication used to treat cancer. It is often administered in combination with other drugs, such as cisplatin, to enhance its effectiveness. One of the notable side effects associated with 5-fluorouracilo is the potential for diarrhea, which can occur during treatment.IRINOTEC√ÅN:Irinotec√°n es un antineopl√°sico que puede causar diarrea como efecto secundario.CAPECITABINA:Capecitabina es un antineopl√°sico que puede estar asociado con la producci√≥n de diarrea.CISPLATINO:Cisplatino is an antineoplastic chemotherapy drug used to treat various types of cancer. It is known to cause several side effects, including diarrhea and hypomagnesemia.ADRIAMICINA:Adriamicina es un antineopl√°sico que puede estar relacionado con la producci√≥n de diarrea.DOCETAXEL:Docetaxel es un antineopl√°sico que puede causar diarrea como efecto secundario.ERLOTINIB:Erlotinib es un antineopl√°sico que puede estar asociado con la producci√≥n de diarrea.GEFITINIB:Gefitinib es un antineopl√°sico que puede causar diarrea como efecto secundario.SORAFENIB:Sorafenib es un antineopl√°sico que puede estar relacionado con la producci√≥n de diarrea.MICOFENOLATO:Micofenolato es un inmunosupresor que puede causar diarrea como efecto secundario.TACROLIMUS:Tacrolimus is an immunosuppressant medication that is known to be associated with the production of diarrhea. Additionally, the levels of Tacrolimus in the body can be influenced by the consumption of grapefruit juice, which may affect its efficacy and safety.SIROLIMUS:Sirolimus es un inmunosupresor que puede causar diarrea como efecto secundario.AMPRENAVIR:Amprenavir es un antirretroviral que puede estar asociado con la producci√≥n de diarrea.SAQUINAVIR:Saquinavir is an antiretroviral medication classified as an HIV protease inhibitor. It is known to potentially cause diarrhea as a side effect. Additionally, the metabolism of Saquinavir can be inhibited by grapefruit juice, which may lead to increased levels of the drug in the body. Conversely, high amounts of garlic can reduce the absorption of Saquinavir, potentially diminishing its effectiveness.NELFINAVIR:Nelfinavir es un antirretroviral que puede estar relacionado con la producci√≥n de diarrea.LOPINAVIR:Lopinavir es un antirretroviral que puede causar diarrea como efecto secundario.)<|COMPLETE|>ENFERMEDAD DE CHAGAS:Enfermedad infecciosa causada por el par√°sito Trypanosoma cruzi, que afecta principalmente a personas en Am√©rica LatinaENFERMEDAD NEUROL√ìGICA:"ENFERMEDAD NEUROL√ìGICA" refers to a broad category of disorders that impact the brain, spinal cord, and nerves. These neurological diseases can result in a range of complications, including dysphagia (difficulty swallowing) and malnutrition, highlighting the significant effects these conditions can have on an individual's overall health and well-being.ENFERMEDAD ENDOCRINA:Disorders that affect the endocrine system, leading to hormonal imbalancesPANHIPOPITUITARISMO:A rare disorder in which the pituitary gland fails to produce sufficient amounts of several hormonesDISTR√ìFIA MIOT√ìNICA:A genetic disorder that affects muscle function and can lead to progressive muscle weaknessESCLEROSIS SIST√âMICA:A chronic autoimmune disease that causes the skin and connective tissues to become thick and hardNADYA:NADYA is a comprehensive group dedicated to the study and support of artificial nutrition, specifically focusing on home and outpatient settings in Spain. The group is involved in both home parenteral nutrition and home enteral nutrition, with a particular emphasis on patients suffering from neurological diseases. Since its establishment in 1992, NADYA has maintained a registry that collects and reports data on patients receiving home parenteral nutrition (NPD), as well as on complications related to enteral nutrition. Through its efforts, NADYA aims to enhance nutritional support and improve outcomes for patients requiring specialized nutritional care.MISOPROSTOL:Misoprostol is a drug used for patients with functional defecation disorders, acting as a prostaglandin analogue.COLCHICINE:Colchicine is a medication used in the treatment of certain conditions affecting bowel function.LUBIPROSTONE:Lubiprostone is a local activator of chloride channels used for treating bowel movement issues.MICROBIOMA INTESTINAL:The "MICROBIOMA INTESTINAL," or human intestinal microbiome, is a significant area of scientific research, particularly concerning its crucial role in health and disease. This microbiome encompasses the genetic makeup of the bacteria residing in the gut, which is essential for various aspects of health and metabolism. Understanding the complexities of the intestinal microbiome is vital for uncovering its impact on overall well-being and the potential implications for various medical conditions.ESTRE√ëIMIENTO CR√ìNICO:Chronic constipation is a long-term condition that affects bowel movements and can lead to various health issues.LAXANTES OSM√ìTICOS:Osmotic laxatives, such as magnesium sulfate and sodium sulfate, work by increasing water retention in the intestines.LAXANTES ESTIMULANTES:Stimulant laxatives, like bisacodyl and senna, stimulate bowel movements by acting on the intestinal nerves.LAXANTES EMOLIENTES:Emollient laxatives, such as docusate sodium, help soften stool by mixing water with fats.LAXANTES QUE AUMENTAN EL BOLO INTESTINAL:Laxatives that increase intestinal bulk, like methylcellulose and psyllium, absorb water to enhance stool volume.DRA. JULIA √ÅLVAREZ:Dra. Julia √Ålvarez is a medical professional who supports the development of young endocrinologists and initiatives in the medical field.LEOPOLDO GARC√çA-VALDECASAS:D. Leopoldo Garc√≠a-Valdecasas is a dedicated member of a team that has contributed to a chapter focused on gastrointestinal health and nutrition. He plays an active role in supporting daily medical initiatives, demonstrating his commitment to advancing knowledge and practices in this important area of health.GLORIA G√ìMEZ-PORTEIRO:Gloria G√≥mez-Porteiro is a dedicated team member actively involved in the development of a chapter focused on gastrointestinal health and nutrition. She contributes significantly to the chapter's medical initiatives, playing a crucial role in advancing its objectives and promoting awareness in this important area of health.ISABEL HIGUERA PULGAR:Isabel Higuera Pulgar is a contributor who played a significant role in the creation of a chapter focused on gastrointestinal health and nutrition. She is part of the team that collaborated on this chapter and actively supports various medical initiatives related to the field.ANA PRIETO:Ana Prieto is a dedicated contributor involved in the creation of a chapter focused on gastrointestinal health and nutrition. As a team member, she plays a significant role in supporting daily medical efforts, demonstrating her commitment to advancing knowledge and practices in this important area of health.MICROBIOMA INTESTINAL HUMANO:SOCIEDAD ESPA√ëOLA DE PROBI√ìTICOS Y PREBI√ìTICOS:The Sociedad Espa√±ola de Probi√≥ticos y Prebi√≥ticos is an organization focused on the scientific evidence of probiotics and prebiotics in health.NUTRICI√ìN EN PATOLOG√çA DEL TUBO DIGESTIVO:"NUTRICI√ìN EN PATOLOG√çA DEL TUBO DIGESTIVO" encompasses a comprehensive examination of nutrition as it relates to various pathologies of the digestive tract. This section emphasizes dietary recommendations specifically tailored for patients suffering from inflammatory bowel disease (EII), addressing the critical role of nutritional management in these cases. It discusses both enteral and parenteral nutrition methods, which are essential for patients facing intestinal issues. Additionally, the content highlights the importance of nutrition in the context of surgical patients and explores various studies and findings that underscore the significance of nutritional management in clinical settings. Overall, the focus is on how effective nutritional strategies can mitigate malnutrition and deficiencies that arise from digestive tract diseases, thereby promoting better gastrointestinal health.HILTON C:Hilton C is a co-author of a study on the variation of bowel habits in two population samples published in the British Medical Journal.IRVINE G:Irvine G is a co-author of a study on the variation of bowel habits in two population samples published in the British Medical Journal.EVERHART JE:Everhart JE is an author of a longitudinal survey of self-reported bowel habits in the United States published in Digestive Diseases and Sciences.GO VL:Go VL is a co-author of a longitudinal survey of self-reported bowel habits in the United States published in Digestive Diseases and Sciences.JOHANNES RS:Johannes RS is a co-author of a longitudinal survey of self-reported bowel habits in the United States published in Digestive Diseases and Sciences.√ÅLVAREZ G:√Ålvarez G is an author of a publication on probiotics, prebiotics, and health by the Sociedad Espa√±ola de Probi√≥ticos y Prebi√≥ticos.MARCOS A:Marcos A is a co-author of a publication on probiotics, prebiotics, and health by the Sociedad Espa√±ola de Probi√≥ticos y Prebi√≥ticos.MARGOLLES A:Margolles A is a co-author of a publication on probiotics, prebiotics, and health by the Sociedad Espa√±ola de Probi√≥ticos y Prebi√≥ticos.GONZ√ÅLEZ-MOLERO I:Gonz√°lez-Molero I is a co-author of an update on probiotics, prebiotics, and symbiotics in clinical nutrition.WONG JMW:Wong JMW is an author of a publication on colonic health and fermentation published in the Journal of Clinical Gastroenterology.RUSSELL DE SOUZA:Russell de Souza is a co-author of a publication on colonic health and fermentation published in the Journal of Clinical Gastroenterology.HOUGHTELING P.D.:Houghteling P.D. is an author of a publication discussing immunohealth, allergies, and enterocolitis.WALKER W.A.:Walker W.A. is a co-author of a publication discussing immunohealth, allergies, and enterocolitis.FLOCH M.H.:Floch M.H. is an author of recommendations for probiotic use published in the Proceedings and Consensus Opinion.EAMONN M. QUIGLEY:Eamonn M. Quigley is an author discussing the role of prebiotics and probiotics in managing gastrointestinal disorders.FARTHING MD:Farthing MD is a co-author of a global perspective on acute diarrhea in adults and children published by WHO.BALFOUR R:Balfour R is an author discussing probiotics for gastrointestinal diseases.ALAM NH:Alam NH is an author of a study on oral rehydration solutions in treating acute diarrhea in children.RAMAKRISHNA BS:Ramakrishna BS is an author of a study on amylase-resistant starch plus oral rehydration solution for cholera.GORE SM:Gore SM is an author of a meta-analysis on the impact of rice-based oral rehydration solutions on diarrhea.PAYNE C:Payne C is an author discussing the pathogenesis of diarrhea in adults.MCFARLAND L:McFarland L is an author discussing irritable bowel syndrome and inflammatory bowel disease research.MALLON P:Mallon P is an author discussing probiotics for the induction of remission in ulcerative colitis.ROLFE VE:Rolfe VE is an author discussing probiotics for the maintenance of remission in Crohn's disease.BUTTERWORTH ANDREW D:Butterworth Andrew D is an author discussing probiotics for the induction of remission in Crohn's disease.)<|COMPLETE|>HOSPITAL UNIVERSITARIO INFANTA ELENA:Hospital Universitario Infanta Elena is a medical institution located in Valdemoro, Madrid. It offers a range of healthcare services and is known for its commitment to providing quality medical care. Teresa de Grado Manchado is one of the professionals working at this hospital, contributing to its operations and patient care.VIRGINIA PE√ëA CORT√âS:Virginia Pe√±a Cort√©s is a medical professional specializing in endocrinology and nutrition at Hospital Virgen de la Salud in Toledo.NOELIA PEL√ÅEZ TORRES:Noelia Pel√°ez Torres is a medical professional in the endocrinology and nutrition section at Hospital Universitario Pr√≠ncipe de Asturias.PANCREATITIS CR√ìNICA:Chronic pancreatitis, known as "pancreatitis cr√≥nica," is a long-term inflammatory condition of the pancreas that results in irreversible structural changes. This chronic inflammation can lead to permanent damage, affecting both the exocrine and endocrine functions of the pancreas. As a consequence, individuals with chronic pancreatitis may experience various digestive issues and impaired insulin production, necessitating nutritional support and careful management of their condition.GL√ÅNDULA PANCRE√ÅTICA:The pancreatic gland is responsible for the secretion of digestive enzymes and hormones such as insulin and glucagon, playing a crucial role in metabolism regulation.ISLOTES DE LANGERHANS:The islets of Langerhans are clusters of cells in the pancreas that produce insulin and glucagon, essential for carbohydrate metabolism regulation.C√ÅLCULOS BILIARES:Gallstones are solid particles that form in the gallbladder and are a leading cause of acute pancreatitis.TUMOR DE PAPILA DUODENAL:Duodenal papilla tumors are another condition that must be considered when diagnosing pancreatitis without a clear cause.DR. JOHN RANSON:Dr. John Ranson established criteria in 1974 to evaluate the severity and prognosis of pancreatitis, identifying patients at high risk of complications.ACUTE PHYSIOLOGY AND CHRONIC HEALTH EVALUATION II:The Acute Physiology and Chronic Health Evaluation II (APACHE II) is a system used to quantify the severity of illness in critically ill patients, which is adjusted with the body mass index.PANCREATITIS ALCOHOLICA:Pancreatitis alcoholica refers to pancreatitis caused by excessive alcohol consumption, with specific criteria for severity.PANCREATITIS BILIAR:Pancreatitis biliar is pancreatitis caused by gallstones, with its own set of severity criteria.BALTHAZAR CLASSIFICATION:The Balthazar classification is a system used to assess the severity of pancreatitis based on imaging findings.LEUCOCITOSIS:Leucocitosis is a condition characterized by an elevated white blood cell count, often observed in patients with pancreatitis as part of the inflammatory response.ECOGRAF√çA ABDOMINAL:Ecograf√≠a abdominal is an imaging technique used to detect alterations in the gallbladder and bile duct, helping to determine the origin of pancreatitis.PANCREATITIS SEVERA NECROTIZANTE:CRITERIOS DE ATLANTA:Los criterios de Atlanta son un conjunto de directrices utilizadas para clasificar la severidad de la pancreatitis aguda.OBSTRUCCI√ìN PARCIAL DEL DUODENO:La obstrucci√≥n parcial del duodeno puede ser una complicaci√≥n de la pancreatitis aguda, afectando la alimentaci√≥n y la absorci√≥n de nutrientes.HIDRATACI√ìN INTRAVENOSA:La hidrataci√≥n intravenosa es un tratamiento utilizado en pacientes con pancreatitis aguda para mantener el equilibrio de l√≠quidos y electrolitos.DISFUNCI√ìN ORG√ÅNICA M√öLTIPLE:A condition where multiple organs do not function properly, often seen in severe cases of acute pancreatitisCORTISOL PLASM√ÅTICO:A hormone that increases in response to stress, often elevated in patients with severe acute pancreatitisHEPATIC STEATOSIS:Hepatic steatosis, or fatty liver, can develop in patients with pancreatitis due to excessive glucose administration.HYPOMAGNESEMIA:Hypomagnesemia is a condition of low magnesium levels in the blood, which can also be seen in patients with pancreatitis.ALGORITMO DEL MANEJO NUTRICIONAL:El algoritmo del manejo nutricional de la pancreatitis aguda es una gu√≠a adaptada para el tratamiento nutricional de pacientes con esta condici√≥n.OLAH:Olah es un autor de un estudio que ha encontrado resultados sobre el soporte nutricional en pacientes con pancreatitis aguda.ABOU-ASSI:Abou-Assi es un autor de un estudio que compara la nutrici√≥n enteral y parenteral en pacientes con pancreatitis aguda.SEPSIS POR CAT√âTER:Sepsis por cat√©ter is a serious complication that can arise in patients receiving parenteral nutrition. This condition is characterized by a severe infection that may occur as a result of the use of central venous catheters. It highlights the risks associated with catheter use in the context of nutritional support, emphasizing the need for careful monitoring and management to prevent such infections.KALFARENTZOS:PANCREATIC DISEASES:Pancreatic diseases refer to conditions affecting the pancreas, which may require nutritional support and management strategies.GANG ZHAO:Gang Zhao is a researcher who conducted a study on the effects of glutamine supplementation in patients with severe pancreatic diseases.PROPATRIA:PROPATRIA is a multicenter, randomized, double-blind study that investigated the effects of probiotics in patients with severe pancreatic diseases.MULTIORGAN FAILURE:Multiorgan failure is a severe condition where multiple organ systems fail, often requiring specialized nutritional management.NUTRITIONAL SUPPORT MIXTURE:CALCIFICACIONES PANCRE√ÅTICAS:Pancreatic calcifications are a classic finding in chronic pancreatitis, indicating permanent damage to the gland.SISTEMA RETICULOENDOTELIAL:The reticuloendothelial system is involved in immune response and may be impacted by chronic pancreatitis.SECRETINA CCK:Secretina CCK is a hormonal test used to assess pancreatic function by stimulating the pancreas and measuring its exocrine reserve.COBALAMINA:Cobalamin, also known as vitamin B12, is a crucial nutrient that can be malabsorbed in patients with pancreatic conditions, leading to deficiencies.ALCOHOLISM:Alcoholism is a chronic condition that significantly impacts health, particularly by exacerbating pancreatic diseases and leading to nutritional deficiencies. It is recognized as the primary etiology of chronic pancreatitis, a serious inflammation of the pancreas. To improve patient outcomes, individuals suffering from chronic alcoholism must achieve absolute abstinence from alcohol.DIEÃÅTICA:Dietary management involves strategies to adjust food intake for patients with pancreatic diseases to alleviate symptoms and improve nutritional status.ESTADO NUTRICIONAL:The "ESTADO NUTRICIONAL" refers to the overall health condition of an individual in relation to their dietary intake and the utilization of nutrients by the body. It encompasses the assessment of how well a person's nutritional needs are being met and how effectively their body absorbs and uses these nutrients. This concept is particularly significant in the context of patients with pancreatic diseases, where nutritional status plays a critical role in their overall health and management.NUTRITIONAL SUPPORT THERAPY:Nutritional Support Therapy is a treatment approach designed to provide adequate nutrition to patients, particularly those who are unable to eat normally. It is a standard practice in the medical field, especially for critically ill patients, where guidelines exist for the provision and assessment of nutrition support therapy. Additionally, Nutritional Support Therapy is recognized as an essential intervention for patients with pancreatitis, ensuring they receive the necessary exogenous nutrients to aid in their recovery.ESTEATORREA:Esteatorrea is a medical condition characterized by the presence of excess fat in the feces, which often indicates underlying malabsorption issues. This condition can be particularly relevant in the context of diabetes management, as it may affect the absorption of nutrients. Esteatorrea is commonly observed in patients with pancreatitis, where malabsorption is a significant concern. Overall, the presence of excess fat in feces serves as an important clinical indicator of digestive health and potential complications related to various medical conditions.SUPORTE M√âDICO-SOCIAL:Soporte m√©dico-social is the medical and social support system that helps patients achieve abstention from alcohol and manage their condition.BLOQUE: NUTRICI√ìN EN PATOLOG√çA DEL TUBO DIGESTIVO:This section discusses nutritional management in digestive tract pathologies, particularly focusing on pancreatitis.ABSTENCI√ìN EN√ìLICA:Abstenci√≥n en√≥lica refers to the cessation of alcohol consumption, which is crucial for managing pancreatitis and preventing further complications.TUBO DIGESTIVO:The "TUBO DIGESTIVO," or digestive tract, is a vital anatomical structure responsible for processing food and facilitating digestion and nutrient absorption. It serves as the pathway through which enteral nutrition is administered directly to patients, highlighting its importance in clinical settings. The functionality of the tubo digestivo is crucial for determining the type of nutritional support required, especially in medical conditions such as pancreatitis, where specific nutritional management is necessary. Additionally, the tubo digestivo can be the subject of various diagnostic explorations to assess its health and functionality. Overall, the tubo digestivo plays a central role in both the digestive process and the management of nutritional needs in patients.DOLORES:AMERICAN COLLEGE OF GASTROENTEROLOGY:The American College of Gastroenterology is a professional organization that provides guidelines for the management of gastrointestinal diseases, including acute pancreatitis.CRITICAL CARE MEDICINE:Critical Care Medicine is a specialized field within medicine that focuses on the diagnosis and management of life-threatening conditions. This specialty encompasses a wide range of severe medical issues, including critical cases such as pancreatitis. Practitioners in Critical Care Medicine often utilize advanced techniques and tools, such as central venous catheters, to provide optimal care for critically ill patients. 

In addition to clinical practice, Critical Care Medicine is also represented in academic literature through a peer-reviewed journal that publishes research findings related to critical care and intensive care medicine. Furthermore, the Society of Critical Care Medicine plays a vital role in this field by providing guidelines and recommendations for the management of critically ill patients, which includes specific protocols for treating patients with burn injuries. Overall, Critical Care Medicine is essential for addressing complex medical emergencies and improving patient outcomes in critical situations.RAN B:Ran B is an author who collaborated on research regarding early severe acute pancreatitis.BERGER HG:Berger HG is an author involved in the study of early severe acute pancreatitis.MITCHELL RM:Mitchell RM is an author who has written about pancreatitis in the Lancet.BYRNE MF:Byrne MF is an author who has contributed to the literature on pancreatitis.BAILLIE J:Baillie J is an author who has published work on pancreatitis.TENNER S:Tenner S is an author who has provided guidelines for the management of acute pancreatitis.DEWITT J:DeWitt J is an author who has contributed to the guidelines on acute pancreatitis.VEGE SS:Vege SS is an author associated with the American College of Gastroenterology guidelines on acute pancreatitis.MEIER RF:Meier RF is an author who has researched nutrition in pancreatic diseases.BEGLINGER:Beglinger is an author who has contributed to the study of nutrition in pancreatic diseases.IMRIE CW:Imrie CW is an author who has researched enteral and parenteral nutrition in acute pancreatitis.CARTER CR:Carter CR is an author who has worked on studies related to acute pancreatitis.MCKAY CJ:McKay CJ is an author who has contributed to the literature on acute pancreatitis.KAGNOFF MF:Kagnoff MF is an author who has researched immunology of the intestinal tract.JABBAR A:Jabbar A is an author who has studied gut immunology and its relation to feeding and starvation.CHANG WK:Chang WK is an author who has researched gut immunology and nutrition.DRYDEN GW:Dryden GW is an author who has contributed to studies on gut immunology.ALVERDY JC:Alverdy JC is an author who has researched the influence of critical illness on gut interactions.SUN JK:Sun JK is an author who has studied the effects of early enteral nutrition on immune function in severe acute pancreatitis patients.GARC√çA-ALONSO FJ:Garc√≠a-Alonso FJ is an author who has researched nutrition in acute pancreatitis.GARRIDO G√ìMEZ E:Garrido G√≥mez E is an author who has contributed to studies on nutrition in acute pancreatitis.P√âREZ-LASALA J:P√©rez-Lasala J is an author who has contributed to studies on nutrition in acute pancreatitis.CANO RUIZ A:Cano Ruiz A is an author who has researched nutrition in acute pancreatitis.MOREIRA VICENTE V:Moreira Vicente V is an author who has studied nutrition in acute pancreatitis.MCLAAVE SA:McClave SA is an author who has published systematic reviews on nutrition support in acute pancreatitis.SITZMANN JV:Sitzmann JV is an author recognized for his research on total parenteral nutrition in patients with pancreatitis. He has specifically studied the use of total parenteral nutrition and alternative energy substrates in the treatment of severe acute pancreatitis, contributing valuable insights to the field.STEINBORN PA:Steinborn PA is an author who has contributed to studies on pancreatitis management.ZINNER MJ:Zinner MJ is an author who has researched surgical management of pancreatitis.ISENMANN R:SURG GYNECOL OBSTET:Surg Gynecol Obstet is a journal that publishes research on surgical and gynecological practices, including nutrition in severe acute pancreatitis.BRITISH JOURNAL OF SURGERY:The British Journal of Surgery (Br J Surg) is a peer-reviewed medical journal dedicated to publishing research on surgical practices and clinical outcomes. It encompasses a wide range of topics within the field of surgery, including studies on nutrition in acute pancreatitis and immunonutrition in gastrointestinal surgery. The journal serves as a platform for disseminating significant findings related to surgical practices, aiming to enhance the understanding and application of surgical techniques and outcomes in the medical community.30TH CONGRESS OF THE EUROPEAN SOCIETY FOR CLINICAL NUTRITION AND METABOLISM:The 30th Congress of the European Society for Clinical Nutrition and Metabolism is a conference focused on advancements in clinical nutrition, including enteral nutrition in severe acute pancreatitis.PITCHUMONI CS:Pitchumoni CS is an author who discussed systemic complications of acute pancreatitis.AL-OMRAN M:Al-Omran M is an author who compared enteral versus parenteral nutrition for acute pancreatitis.OLAH A:Olah A is an author who studied early nasojejunal feeding in acute pancreatitis and its association with lower complication rates.ZHU Y:Zhu Y is an author who conducted a meta-analysis on nasogastric versus nasojejunal nutrition in patients with severe acute pancreatitis.SWAROOP VS:Swaroop VS is an author who wrote about severe acute pancreatitis.MEIER R:Meier R is an author who studied the effects of enteral fish oil in acute pancreatitis.MCNAUGHT CE:McNaught CE is an author who conducted a prospective randomized trial of probiotics in critically ill patients.GASTROENTEROL RES PRACT:AMERICAN JOURNAL OF GASTROENTEROLOGY:The American Journal of Gastroenterology publishes research and reviews on gastrointestinal diseases, including chronic pancreatitis.PANCREATOLOGY:Pancreatology is a journal dedicated to the study of the pancreas and its diseases, including pancreatitis.CHRONIC PANCREATITIS:Chronic pancreatitis is a long-term inflammatory condition of the pancreas that can lead to pain and digestive issues.MAYER K:Mayer K is a researcher who has contributed to studies on the effects of nutritional interventions in pancreatitis patients.FOITZIK T:Foitzik T is a researcher who has published work on the effects of omega-3 fatty acids in pancreatitis.SHEA JC:Shea JC is a researcher focused on enteral therapy and its effects on chronic pancreatitis.IHSE I:Ihse I is a researcher who has contributed to guidelines for the management of chronic pancreatitis.HOFFMEISTER A:Hoffmeister A is a researcher involved in the development of consensus guidelines for chronic pancreatitis.TROLLI PA:Trolli PA is a researcher who has studied pancreatic enzyme therapy and its effects on patients with chronic pancreatitis.BESSELINK MG:EDUARDO PLATERO RODRIGO:Eduardo Platero Rodrigo is a member of the Endocrinology and Nutrition Section at the University Hospital in Guadalajara.√ÅLVARO GARC√çA-MANZANARES V√ÅZQUEZ DE AGREDOS:√Ålvaro Garc√≠a-Manzanares V√°zquez de Agredos is a member of the Endocrinology and Nutrition Section at HG La Mancha Centro in Alc√°zar de San Juan.NURIA GIL FOURNIER:Nuria Gil Fournier is a member of the Endocrinology and Nutrition Section at the General Hospital of Villalba in Madrid.HOSPITAL UNIVERSITARIO:The University Hospital is a medical institution where Eduardo Platero Rodrigo works, focusing on endocrinology and nutrition.HG LA MANCHA CENTRO:HG La Mancha Centro is a medical institution where √Ålvaro Garc√≠a-Manzanares V√°zquez de Agredos works, focusing on endocrinology and nutrition.FISIOPATOLOG√çA:Pathophysiology involves the study of the functional changes that occur in the body as a result of a disease, such as inflammatory bowel disease.SUR DE ESPA√ëA:The southern region of Spain, where a study on the incidence of inflammatory bowel disease was conducted.NORTE DE AM√âRICA:North America, a region associated with high rates of incidence and prevalence of inflammatory bowel disease.)<|COMPLETE|>MYCOBACTERIUM AVIUM SUBESPECIES PARATUBERCULOSIS:Mycobacterium avium subspecies paratuberculosis is a bacterium that has been studied for its potential link to inflammatory bowel diseases, including Crohn's disease.HELICOBACTER HEPATICUS:Helicobacter hepaticus is a bacterium that has been studied for its role in gastrointestinal diseases, including its potential association with inflammatory bowel disease.BACTEROIDES VULGATUS:Bacteroides vulgatus is a bacterium that has been implicated in gastrointestinal health and disease, particularly in relation to inflammatory bowel disease.ANTICUERPOS ANTICITOPLASMA DE NEUTR√ìFILOS:Anticuerpos anticitoplasma de neutr√≥filos (p-ANCA) are antibodies that are often present in patients with ulcerative colitis, indicating an autoimmune response.ANTICUERPOS ANTI-SACCHAROMYCES CEREVISIAE:Anticuerpos anti-Saccharomyces cerevisiae (ASCA) are antibodies associated with Crohn's disease, indicating a potential relationship with inflammatory bowel disease.GEN NOD-2/CARD15:The NOD-2/CARD15 gene is associated with the immune response and has been linked to the development of Crohn's disease.SULFASALACINA:Sulfasalacina is a medication primarily utilized as a first-line treatment for ulcerative colitis, where it plays a crucial role in reducing inflammation. Additionally, it is important to note that sulfasalacina can interfere with the absorption of nutrients in patients suffering from inflammatory bowel disease. This dual function highlights both its therapeutic benefits and potential side effects in managing gastrointestinal conditions.AMINOSALICILATOS:Aminosalicylic drugs are used in the treatment of ulcerative colitis and Crohn's disease to maintain remission and reduce inflammation.TENESMO:Tenesmus is a symptom characterized by a constant feeling of needing to pass stools, often associated with colitis ulcerosa.URGENCIA DEPOSICIONAL:Urgency of defecation is a symptom that can occur in patients with colitis ulcerosa, indicating inflammation of the rectum.CU:CU refers to Colitis Ulcerosa, also known as ulcerative colitis, which is a chronic inflammatory bowel disease that primarily affects the colon. This condition is characterized by acute flare-ups and can lead to severe malnutrition if not properly managed. Treatment is essential to alleviate symptoms and maintain remission. Additionally, it is important to note that "CU" can also refer to copper, an essential trace element required in small amounts for various biological functions, particularly in the context of parenteral nutrition. However, in the context of the provided descriptions, CU predominantly pertains to Colitis Ulcerosa.EC:EC, or Enfermedad de Crohn, is a type of inflammatory bowel disease characterized by its chronic nature. This condition can lead to malnutrition and necessitates a variety of treatment approaches to manage its symptoms and complications.BUDESONIDA:Budesonida is a corticosteroid that helps suppress inflammation in patients with inflammatory bowel disease.CLARITROMICINA:Claritromicina is an antibiotic that may be used in the treatment of severe inflammatory bowel disease.METRONIDAZOL:Metronidazol is an antibiotic that is utilized to treat a variety of infections, particularly those caused by anaerobic bacteria. It is indicated for severe forms of inflammatory bowel disease, especially in cases involving perianal complications. Additionally, metronidazol is effective in addressing bacterial overgrowth in patients receiving parenteral nutrition. The medication also has the capability to inhibit aldehyde dehydrogenase, which can impact alcohol metabolism.INFLIXIMAB:Infliximab is a biological therapy that targets tumor necrosis factor (TNF) and is used in the treatment of inflammatory bowel disease.ADALIMUMAB:Adalimumab is a monoclonal antibody used in the treatment of inflammatory bowel disease, particularly effective against TNF.GOLIMUMAB:Golimumab is another anti-TNF monoclonal antibody used in the management of inflammatory bowel disease.CERTOLIZUMAB:Certolizumab is a biological agent that targets TNF and is used in the treatment of inflammatory bowel disease.VEDOLIZUMAB:Vedolizumab is a monoclonal antibody used to treat inflammatory bowel disease by targeting specific integrins involved in inflammation.INMUNOMODULADORES:Immunomodulators such as 6-mercaptopurina, azatioprina, and metotrexato are used for maintenance treatment in inflammatory bowel disease, particularly when other treatments fail.TERAPIAS BIOLOGICAS:Biological therapies, including monoclonal antibodies against TNF, have revolutionized the treatment of inflammatory bowel disease, providing new options for management.DEP:Deficiencia Energ√©tico-Prot√©ica, un estado de desnutrici√≥n que puede ocurrir en pacientes con enfermedad inflamatoria intestinalDIETA RESTRICTIVA:Una dieta que limita ciertos alimentos, que puede contribuir a la desnutrici√≥n en pacientes con enfermedad inflamatoria intestinalSANGRE:P√©rdida de sangre gastrointestinal que puede ocurrir en pacientes con enfermedad inflamatoria intestinal, contribuyendo a la desnutrici√≥nESTR√âS PSICOSOCIAL:El estr√©s psicosocial se asocia con la EII, manifest√°ndose en ansiedad y depresi√≥n, especialmente en adultos y ni√±os."N-TELOP√âPTIDO DE COL√ÅGENO TIPO I:El N-telop√©ptido de col√°geno tipo I es un marcador de resorci√≥n √≥sea que se mide en orina en pacientes con enfermedad inflamatoria intestinal.SIALOPROTE√çNA √ìSEA:La sialoprote√≠na √≥sea es un marcador utilizado para evaluar la resorci√≥n √≥sea en pacientes con enfermedad inflamatoria intestinal.FOSFATASA ALCALINA √ìSEA:La fosfatasa alcalina √≥sea es un marcador que se utiliza para evaluar la salud √≥sea en pacientes con enfermedad inflamatoria intestinal.EII:EII refers to inflammatory bowel disease, encompassing conditions such as Crohn's disease and ulcerative colitis that affect the digestive tract.BIFOSFONATOS:Bisphosphonates are a class of medications approved by the FDA for the prevention of osteoporosis. They are specifically indicated for use in patients with osteopenia, as they help to reduce bone resorption markers. These medications are prescribed at specific dosages to effectively manage and treat conditions related to bone density loss.B12:Vitamin B12 is a vitamin that may be supplemented in high doses for patients with moderate deficiencies.FLORA INTESTINAL:Intestinal flora refers to the community of microorganisms in the gut, which can be altered in patients with EII and affect lactose digestion.OLESTRA:Olestra es un sustituto de grasa que ha sido aprobado por la FDA y se utiliza en productos alimenticios para reducir el contenido cal√≥rico.COLLESTERAMINA:La colesteramina es un medicamento que se utiliza para reducir los niveles de colesterol en la sangre y puede afectar la absorci√≥n de grasas.F√çSTULAS ENTEROCUT√ÅNEAS:F√≠stulas enterocut√°neas are abnormal connections between the intestine and the skin that can complicate nutritional management in patients. These fistulas can lead to severe malnutrition due to the loss of intestinal contents and impaired nutrient absorption. Treatment options for f√≠stulas enterocut√°neas may include nutritional support through Total Parenteral Nutrition (NPT), provided that certain conditions are met.ACEITES DE OLIVA:Tipo de aceite utilizado en dietas enterales polim√©ricas que puede ser beneficioso para pacientes con enfermedad inflamatoria intestinalCRECIMIENTO:Proceso biol√≥gico que puede requerir un aumento en la ingesta nutricional, especialmente en ni√±os y adolescentesOSTOM√çAS:OSTOM√çAS are surgical procedures that involve creating an opening, known as a stoma, to allow for the discharge of body wastes. These procedures are often necessary for patients with conditions such as POIC (P√©rdida de Oclusi√≥n Intestinal Cr√≥nica) to facilitate the drainage of intestinal contents and support long-term enteral nutrition. Ostom√≠as can significantly impact a patient's nutritional status and may require careful evaluation, sometimes involving contrast administration. While these surgical openings serve essential functions for waste elimination and feeding, they can also lead to complications that need to be managed. Overall, ostom√≠as are critical interventions that provide necessary support for individuals with specific medical needs.S√çNDROME SUBOCLUSIVO:Sindrome suboclusivo is a condition that may be managed with NPT and digestive aspiration to avoid surgery.LACTOBACILLI:Lactobacilli are a type of probiotic bacteria that can have beneficial effects on gut health.VSL-3:VSL-3 is a specific probiotic formulation that contains a mixture of eight different bacterial strains. It is recognized for its effectiveness in managing gastrointestinal health, particularly in conditions such as ulcerative colitis.CORTICOESTEROIDES:Corticosteroids are anti-inflammatory medications often used in the treatment of IBD to reduce inflammation and manage symptoms.INFECCIONES POSTOPERATORIAS:Postoperative infections are complications that can arise after surgery, which may be influenced by nutritional status and treatment methods.DA√ëO DEL CONDUCTO LINF√ÅTICO:Lymphatic duct damage can occur during medical procedures and may complicate nutritional treatments like NPT.DEFICIT DE COBRE:Copper deficiency is a potential complication of long-term nutritional treatments that require monitoring of micronutrient levels.ENCEFALOPAT√çA DE WERNICKE:Wernicke's encephalopathy is a neurological condition caused by thiamine deficiency, which can be a risk in patients receiving certain nutritional therapies.BERI-BERI:Beri-beri is a disease caused by thiamine deficiency, which can occur in patients with inadequate nutritional support.)<|COMPLETE|>SYMBIOTICS:Symbiotics are combinations of probiotics and prebiotics that may enhance the health benefits of both.ENFERMEDADES INFLAMATORIAS INTESTINALES:Enfermedades Inflamatorias Intestinales son condiciones que afectan el tubo digestivo, requiriendo atenci√≥n m√©dica y nutricional especial. Estas enfermedades pueden provocar desnutrici√≥n y d√©ficits de micronutrientes, lo que subraya la importancia de un manejo adecuado y un enfoque integral en su tratamiento.IL-10:IL-10 es una interleucina que juega un papel en la inmunorregulaci√≥n y es inducida en el contexto de enfermedades inflamatorias intestinales.IGA:IgA es un tipo de inmunoglobulina cuya secreci√≥n es estimulada en el contexto de enfermedades inflamatorias intestinales.IGE:IgE es una inmunoglobulina cuya producci√≥n es inhibida en el contexto de enfermedades inflamatorias intestinales.SARTOR ET AL.:CORTICOIDEO:El tratamiento corticoideo se utiliza en pacientes con enfermedades inflamatorias intestinales para controlar la inflamaci√≥n.COLITIS ULCERATIVA:La colitis ulcerativa es otra forma de enfermedad inflamatoria intestinal que afecta el colon y el recto.COLOMBEL JF:Colombel JF is a co-author of a review on indeterminate colitis, providing insights into inflammatory bowel diseases.GREENSTEIN A:Greenstein A is a researcher who contributed to the study of indeterminate colitis, focusing on inflammatory bowel diseases.STANGE EF:Stange EF is a co-author of the European evidence-based Consensus on the diagnosis and management of ulcerative colitis.TRAVIS SP:Travis SP is a co-author of the European evidence-based Consensus on ulcerative colitis, contributing to its management guidelines.VERMEIRE S:Vermeire S is a co-author of the European evidence-based Consensus on ulcerative colitis, focusing on diagnosis and management.BERNSTEIN CN:Bernstein CN is a researcher who has studied the epidemiology of Crohn's disease and ulcerative colitis in Canada.DESAI HG:Desai HG is a researcher who has investigated the increasing incidence of Crohn's disease in India.GARC√çA DE TENA J:Garc√≠a de Tena J is an author who has written about the etiopathogenesis of inflammatory bowel diseases.SARTOR RB:Sartor RB is a researcher who has focused on therapeutic manipulation of the enteric microflora in inflammatory bowel diseases.SANDS BE:Sands BE is a researcher who has contributed to the understanding of clinical distinctions among various forms of intestinal inflammation.KLEMENT E:Klement E is a researcher who has studied the association between childhood hygiene and the risk of inflammatory bowel disease.EDWARD V:Edward V is a researcher who has focused on the clinical epidemiology of inflammatory bowel disease.VAN ASSCHE G:Van Assche G is a co-author of the second European evidence-based Consensus on Crohn's disease.MENCH√âN L:Mench√©n L is a researcher who has studied osteoporosis in relation to inflammatory bowel disease.SILBERMINTZ A:Silbermintz A is a researcher who has explored the use of capsule endoscopy in evaluating Crohn's disease.GOMOLL√ìN F:Gomoll√≥n F is a prominent representative of GETECCU (the Spanish Group for Working on Crohn's Disease and Ulcerative Colitis) and has made significant contributions to the therapeutic guidelines concerning ulcerative colitis. Through this role, Gomoll√≥n F plays an important part in advancing the understanding and treatment of inflammatory bowel diseases in Spain.GEBEES K:GETECCU:GETECCU is the Spanish Group for Working on Crohn's Disease and Ulcerative Colitis, which develops therapeutic guidelines for these conditions.HANAUER SB:Hanauer SB is an author who has written about medical therapy for ulcerative colitis.SOLINA G:Solina G is an author discussing the current management of intestinal bowel disease and the role of surgery.MART√çNEZ-MONTIEL MP:Mart√≠nez-Montiel MP is an author who has written about biologic therapies for chronic inflammatory bowel disease.MANTEJO A:Mantejo A is an author who has contributed to the understanding of nutritional support in inflammatory bowel disease.BA√ëOS R:Ba√±os R is an author who has researched lactose malabsorption in patients with inactive inflammatory bowel disease.GARC√çA-PLANELLA E:CMAJ:CMAJ, or the Canadian Medical Association Journal, is a peer-reviewed medical journal that focuses on publishing research, guidelines, and reviews in various fields of medicine. It covers a wide range of topics, including clinical nutrition, health, fitness, and frailty, particularly in elderly populations. Through its publications, CMAJ aims to contribute to the advancement of medical knowledge and practice in Canada and beyond.NUTRITION CLINICAL:Nutrition Clinical refers to the clinical aspects of nutrition management in patients with gastrointestinal diseases.BLASCO ML:Blasco ML is an author who contributed to the research on inflammatory bowel disease.GIM√âNEZ:Gim√©nez is an author mentioned in the context of nutritional support for inflammatory bowel disease.GIMENO V:Gimeno V is an author involved in the study of inflammatory bowel disease.OLIVER V:Oliver V is an author who has contributed to the research on inflammatory bowel disease.PE√ëA A:Pe√±a A is an author referenced in the context of inflammatory bowel disease research.JEEJEEBHOY KN:Jeejeebhoy KN is an author who has written about clinical nutrition and Crohn's disease management.BUTLER CC:Butler CC is an author who conducted a systematic review on vitamin B12 deficiency treatment.VIDAL-ALABALL J:Vidal-Alaball J is an author involved in the research on vitamin B12 deficiency.CANNINGS-JOHN R:Cannings-John R is an author who contributed to the study of vitamin B12 treatment.MCCADDON A:McCaddon A is an author who has researched vitamin B12 deficiency management.HOOD K:Hood K is an author involved in the systematic review of vitamin B12 treatment.PAPAIOANNOU A:Papaioannou A is an author who contributed to the research on vitamin B12 deficiency.MCDOWELL I:McDowell I is an author who has researched vitamin B12 deficiency treatment.GORINGE A:Goringe A is a researcher and author who has made significant contributions to the fields of parenteral glutamine in bone marrow transplantation and vitamin B12 deficiency. Through their work, Goringe A has explored the implications of parenteral glutamine in enhancing outcomes for patients undergoing bone marrow transplantation, while also investigating the effects and treatment of vitamin B12 deficiency.WƒòDRYCHOWICZ A:Wƒôdrychowicz A is an author who has reviewed advances in nutritional therapy for inflammatory bowel diseases.ZAJƒÑC A:ZajƒÖc A is an author who has contributed to the review of nutritional therapy in inflammatory bowel diseases.TOMASIK P:Tomasik P is an author involved in the review of nutritional therapy for inflammatory bowel diseases.ZACHOS M:Zachos M is an author who has researched enteral nutritional therapy for Crohn's disease.TONDEUR M:Tondeur M is an author who has studied enteral nutritional therapy for Crohn's disease.GRIFFITHS AM:Griffiths AM is an author who has researched enteral nutritional therapy for Crohn's disease.PHILLIPE MARTEAU:Phillipe Marteau is an author who has written about enteral nutrition in Crohn's disease management.ESTEVE-COMAS M:Esteve-Comas M is an author involved in the study of enteral nutrition for Crohn's disease.ABAD LACRUZ A:Abad Lacruz A is an author who has contributed to the research on enteral nutrition in Crohn's disease.ACERO D:Acero D is an author involved in the study of enteral nutrition for Crohn's disease.SANDERSON I R:Sanderson I R is an author who has discussed the anti-inflammatory effects of enteral nutrition.CROFT N M:Croft N M is an author who has researched the anti-inflammatory effects of enteral nutrition.CAMPOS FG:Campos FG is an author who has studied pharmacological nutrition in inflammatory bowel diseases.WAITZBERG DL:Waitzberg DL is an author involved in the research on pharmacological nutrition for inflammatory bowel diseases.TEXEIRA MG:Texeira MG is an author who has contributed to the study of pharmacological nutrition in inflammatory bowel diseases.MUCERINO DR:Mucerino DR is an author involved in the research on pharmacological nutrition for inflammatory bowel diseases.KISS DR:Kiss DR is an author who has studied pharmacological nutrition in inflammatory bowel diseases.HABR-GAMA A:Habr-Gama A is an author involved in the research on pharmacological nutrition for inflammatory bowel diseases.PHILIPSEN-GEERLING BJ:Philipsen-Geerling BJ is a researcher and author who has made significant contributions to studies on nutrition in Crohn's disease. Their work focuses on understanding the nutritional aspects and implications for individuals affected by this condition.BRUMMER RJM:Brummer RJM is a researcher specializing in clinical nutrition and metabolism. He is also an author who focuses on the study of nutrition in relation to Crohn's disease. Through his work, Brummer RJM contributes to the understanding of how nutritional factors can impact metabolic processes and the management of specific health conditions, particularly Crohn's disease.PEARSON M:Pearson M is a researcher and author who has focused on the study of food intolerance and its relationship to Crohn's disease. Through their research, Pearson M has contributed valuable insights into how food intolerance may impact individuals suffering from this inflammatory bowel condition.TEAHON K:Teahon K is a researcher and author who has made significant contributions to the study of Crohn's disease. Their work encompasses research on the disease itself as well as the exploration of food intolerance in relation to Crohn's disease, highlighting their multifaceted involvement in this area of medical research.LEVI AJ:Levi AJ is a researcher and author who is actively involved in the study of Crohn's disease. He has made significant contributions to the understanding of food intolerance in relation to this condition, enhancing the body of research surrounding both Crohn's disease and dietary factors that may influence its management.BJARNASON I:Bjarnason I is a researcher and author who has focused on the study of food intolerance and its effects on Crohn's disease. Through his research, he has explored the relationship between food intolerance and the management of this chronic inflammatory bowel condition, contributing valuable insights to the field.GERBER P. FORMULAS:Gerber P. Formulas is a brand known for its nutritional products, particularly those containing live probiotic bacteria.E. CABR√â GELADA:E. Cabr√© Gelada is a researcher who has written about nutrition and inflammatory bowel disease.COMPLEJO HOSPITALARIO UNIVERSITARIO ALBACETE:The Complejo Hospitalario Universitario Albacete is a healthcare institution where research and clinical nutrition services are provided.NUTRICI√ìN EN CROHN'S DISEASE:FALLO INTESTINAL TIPO II:El fallo intestinal tipo II es una condici√≥n m√©dica que ocurre tras cat√°strofes abdominales y complicaciones quir√∫rgicas, resultando en la necesidad de resecciones intestinales extensas o la aparici√≥n de f√≠stulas.INGLATERRA:Inglaterra es un pa√≠s donde se ha estimado una incidencia anual de fallo intestinal tipo II de 9 casos por mill√≥n de habitantes.TRAUMATISMOS:TRAUMATISMOS refer to severe physical injuries that necessitate medical attention and may benefit from immunomodulatory treatments. These injuries can impact the intestines, leading to conditions that require nutritional support, such as parenteral nutrition. Additionally, TRAUMATISMOS are recognized as one of the potential causes of type II intestinal failure, which may sometimes require extensive intestinal resections. In certain cases, surgical interventions, such as faringostom√≠a, may be necessary to provide feeding access for affected individuals.ISQUEMIA INTESTINAL:Ischemia intestinal is a medical condition characterized by insufficient blood flow to the intestines. This condition can arise as a rare complication in critically ill patients and is particularly concerning for those receiving nutritional support. Ischemia intestinal can lead to intestinal failure type II, which significantly impacts the circulation within the intestines. The reduction in blood flow can result in serious complications, highlighting the importance of monitoring and managing this condition in vulnerable patient populations.F√çSTULA:Una f√≠stula es una conexi√≥n an√≥mala entre dos estructuras epiteliales o cavidades, que puede ser una complicaci√≥n del fallo intestinal.OBSTRUCCI√ìN MEC√ÅNICA:La obstrucci√≥n mec√°nica es una de las causas que pueden llevar al fallo intestinal, afectando el tr√°nsito intestinal.ENFERMEDAD EXTENSA DE LA MUCOSA:La enfermedad extensa de la mucosa es una condici√≥n que puede contribuir al fallo intestinal, afectando la absorci√≥n de nutrientes.DISMOTILIDAD INTESTINAL:La dismotilidad intestinal es un trastorno que puede causar fallo intestinal, afectando la motilidad del intestino.DEHISCENCIA DE SUTURAS:F√çSTULA ENTERO-CUT√ÅNEA:Una f√≠stula entero-cut√°nea (FEC) es un tipo espec√≠fico de f√≠stula que conecta el tracto gastrointestinal intraabdominal con el exterior del cuerpo, a menudo resultando de condiciones m√©dicas severas.POIC:Pseudoobstrucci√≥n intestinal cr√≥nica (POIC) is a rare and severe disorder that simulates intestinal obstruction without a fixed anatomical cause. It is characterized by chronic symptoms such as abdominal pain and vomiting, which can lead to significant issues with intestinal motility. Due to its nonspecific symptoms, POIC often results in a long diagnostic delay, necessitating a high level of suspicion and the exclusion of mechanical obstruction for accurate diagnosis. The condition can severely impact patients' nutritional status, often requiring nutritional support and specific management strategies. Additionally, POIC is sometimes associated with Short Bowel Syndrome, highlighting the need for education and tailored nutritional care for affected individuals.ENFERMEDAD DE HIRSCHSPRUNG:La enfermedad de Hirschsprung es una condici√≥n cong√©nita que afecta la motilidad intestinal, ocurriendo en aproximadamente uno de cada 6000 nacidos y puede llevar a complicaciones severas.VIRUS NEUROTROPOS:Los virus neurotropos, como el herpesvirus y el virus JC, han sido implicados en la etiolog√≠a de la pseudoobstrucci√≥n intestinal cr√≥nica, afectando el sistema nervioso y la funci√≥n intestinal.ENFERMEDADES GRANULOMATOSAS:Las enfermedades granulomatosas, como la tuberculosis, pueden causar f√≠stulas intestinales, complicando el manejo cl√≠nico del paciente.NEUROPAT√çAS:Las neuropat√≠as son condiciones que pueden causar problemas en la motilidad intestinal, contribuyendo a la pseudoobstrucci√≥n intestinal cr√≥nica en algunos pacientes.TRASTORNOS ESPEC√çFICOS DE LA POIC:Los trastornos espec√≠ficos de la POIC incluyen complicaciones como deshidrataci√≥n y alteraciones electrol√≠ticas, que son relevantes para el manejo de esta condici√≥n.)<|COMPLETE|>V√ÅLVULA ILEOCECAL:La v√°lvula ileocecal regula el paso de contenido al colon y act√∫a como barrera entre el colon y el intestino delgado.INTENSIVE NUTRITIONAL SUPPORT:Intensive nutritional support is a treatment approach for patients with intestinal failure to maintain nutritional status and prevent malnutrition.ADAPTATION:Adaptation is a biological process where the remaining intestine adjusts to take over the functions of the lost intestine, enhancing nutrient absorption.CHILDREN:Children are individuals in the developmental stage from birth to adolescence, characterized by their unique nutritional needs and vulnerability to malnutrition and growth issues. During this early stage of life, children may require specialized nutritional support and solutions to ensure their health and proper development. Additionally, children possess a greater capacity for intestinal adaptation, particularly following extensive resections of the intestine, which highlights their resilience and adaptability during this critical period of growth.DIGESTIVE SECRETIONS:Digestive secretions are fluids produced by the digestive system that aid in the breakdown and absorption of nutrients.ANATOMY:Anatomy refers to the structure of the body and its parts, playing a vital role in various medical contexts. It is essential for understanding the implications of intestinal loss in patients with Short Bowel Syndrome (SIC), as well as for determining the most suitable sites for venous access. This knowledge of anatomical structures is crucial for effective medical interventions and patient care.FLUIDS:CINE-RM:Cine-RM is an emerging technique for diagnosing intestinal pathologies, particularly useful in the context of POIC.FALLO INTESTINAL AGUDO:Fallo intestinal agudo is a critical condition requiring investigation of underlying causes such as electrolyte imbalances, pancreatitis, or sepsis.TR√ÅNSITO INTESTINAL:Tr√°nsito intestinal is a diagnostic procedure involving the use of contrast to assess the length of the remaining intestine and its functionality.FEC:FEC, which stands for Enterocutaneous Fistula, is a medical condition characterized by an abnormal connection between the gastrointestinal tract and the skin. This condition, also referred to as "fistula entero-cut√°nea" or "f√≠stula enteral cr√≥nica," necessitates careful nutritional management due to its catabolic nature. Patients with FEC often require nutritional support, which may involve the use of enteral or parenteral nutrition, as the condition can lead to significant challenges in nutrient absorption. Additionally, FEC is associated with chronic intestinal failure, where the intestines are unable to adequately absorb nutrients, further emphasizing the need for medical intervention and comprehensive management strategies.GATORADE:Gatorade is a commercial sports drink that is often misunderstood as isotonic but is actually hypotonic.SUERORAL:Sueroral is a type of oral rehydration solution that contains sodium and is used for hydration.SUERORAL HIPOS√ìDICO:Sueroral hipos√≥dico is a low-sodium oral rehydration solution.LIQUIDOS HIPOTONICOS:Hypotonic liquids are solutions that have a lower sodium content and can also increase net digestive losses.CAPSULA DE CLORURO SODICO:A capsule containing sodium chloride that may be recommended for patients to take with isotonic liquids to avoid complete restriction of hypotonic liquids.DIETA BAJA EN LACTOSA:A low-lactose diet is recommended for patients to optimize intestinal motility and reduce the risk of bacterial overgrowth.LIQUIDOS HIPERTONICOS:LIQUIDOS ISOTONICOS:PACIENTES CON FALLA INTESTINAL:Patients suffering from intestinal failure, either acute or chronic, who require nutritional support to manage their condition.NUTRICI√ìN HYPERF√ÅGICA:A dietary approach that involves providing a high-calorie intake to patients with reduced absorptive capacity.NUTRICI√ìN POLIM√âRICA:A type of enteral nutrition formula that contains intact macronutrients, used for patients with some digestive capacity.(N␀␀␀␀␀␀≈N␀␀␀␀␀␀oO␀␀␀␀␀␀ÙO␀␀␀␀␀␀fP␀␀␀␀␀␀÷P␀␀␀␀␀␀IQ␀␀␀␀␀␀NR␀␀␀␀␀␀ΩR␀␀␀␀␀␀%S␀␀␀␀␀␀§S␀␀␀␀␀␀T␀␀␀␀␀␀~T␀␀␀␀␀␀ÌT␀␀␀␀␀␀cU␀␀␀␀␀␀ËU␀␀␀␀␀␀UV␀␀␀␀␀␀ŸV␀␀␀␀␀␀pW␀␀␀␀␀␀ﬂW␀␀␀␀␀␀YX␀␀␀␀␀␀ŸX␀␀␀␀␀␀[Y␀␀␀␀␀␀œY␀␀␀␀␀␀5Z␀␀␀␀␀␀¨Z␀␀␀␀␀␀[␀␀␀␀␀␀d[␀␀␀␀␀␀\␀␀␀␀␀␀ô\␀␀␀␀␀␀.]␀␀␀␀␀␀≤]␀␀␀␀␀␀h^␀␀␀␀␀␀Ì^␀␀␀␀␀␀h_␀␀␀␀␀␀Œ_␀␀␀␀␀␀6`␀␀␀␀␀␀ê`␀␀␀␀␀␀ub␀␀␀␀␀␀°c␀␀␀␀␀␀d␀␀␀␀␀␀sd␀␀␀␀␀␀ﬂd␀␀␀␀␀␀<e␀␀␀␀␀␀ée␀␀␀␀␀␀‡e␀␀␀␀␀␀Zf␀␀␀␀␀␀ƒf␀␀␀␀␀␀Kg␀␀␀␀␀␀∞g␀␀␀␀␀␀h␀␀␀␀␀␀Åh␀␀␀␀␀␀0i␀␀␀␀␀␀£i␀␀␀␀␀␀j␀␀␀␀␀␀tj␀␀␀␀␀␀Õj␀␀␀␀␀␀0k␀␀␀␀␀␀õk␀␀␀␀␀␀l␀␀␀␀␀␀äl␀␀␀␀␀␀ˇl␀␀␀␀␀␀om␀␀␀␀␀␀n␀␀␀␀␀␀™n␀␀␀␀␀␀So␀␀␀␀␀␀“o␀␀␀␀␀␀\p␀␀␀␀␀␀◊p␀␀␀␀␀␀Íq␀␀␀␀␀␀¥r␀␀␀␀␀␀‹s␀␀␀␀␀␀iu␀␀␀␀␀␀v␀␀␀␀␀␀õv␀␀␀␀␀␀⁄x␀␀␀␀␀␀Ey␀␀␀␀␀␀Úy␀␀␀␀␀␀Üz␀␀␀␀␀␀{␀␀␀␀␀␀í|␀␀␀␀␀␀ˆ|␀␀␀␀␀␀ô}␀␀␀␀␀␀~␀␀␀␀␀␀o~␀␀␀␀␀␀’~␀␀␀␀␀␀Ä␀␀␀␀␀␀Ä␀␀␀␀␀␀’Ä␀␀␀␀␀␀ìÅ␀␀␀␀␀␀XÑ␀␀␀␀␀␀œÖ␀␀␀␀␀␀Lá␀␀␀␀␀␀ﬁá␀␀␀␀␀␀äà␀␀␀␀␀␀Dâ␀␀␀␀␀␀«â␀␀␀␀␀␀?ä␀␀␀␀␀␀Âä␀␀␀␀␀␀kã␀␀␀␀␀␀˛ã␀␀␀␀␀␀\ç␀␀␀␀␀␀⁄é␀␀␀␀␀␀Zê␀␀␀␀␀␀Ïê␀␀␀␀␀␀+ì␀␀␀␀␀␀Kì␀␀␀␀␀␀˚ì␀␀␀␀␀␀vî␀␀␀␀␀␀¸î␀␀␀␀␀␀âï␀␀␀␀␀␀Ùï␀␀␀␀␀␀sñ␀␀␀␀␀␀„ñ␀␀␀␀␀␀Yó␀␀␀␀␀␀‘ó␀␀␀␀␀␀Vò␀␀␀␀␀␀Ωò␀␀␀␀␀␀Äö␀␀␀␀␀␀4õ␀␀␀␀␀␀Óõ␀␀␀␀␀␀Eù␀␀␀␀␀␀û␀␀␀␀␀␀ßû␀␀␀␀␀␀Dü␀␀␀␀␀␀Ÿ†␀␀␀␀␀␀{°␀␀␀␀␀␀9£␀␀␀␀␀␀	ß␀␀␀␀␀␀©␀␀␀␀␀␀™©␀␀␀␀␀␀0™␀␀␀␀␀␀§¨␀␀␀␀␀␀_≠␀␀␀␀␀␀j≠␀␀␀␀␀␀Ê≠␀␀␀␀␀␀êÆ␀␀␀␀␀␀Ø␀␀␀␀␀␀éØ␀␀␀␀␀␀∞␀␀␀␀␀␀Ø∞␀␀␀␀␀␀ø∞␀␀␀␀␀␀â≥␀␀␀␀␀␀¥␀␀␀␀␀␀ú¥␀␀␀␀␀␀7µ␀␀␀␀␀␀‰µ␀␀␀␀␀␀t∂␀␀␀␀␀␀9∑␀␀␀␀␀␀‡∑␀␀␀␀␀␀Èπ␀␀␀␀␀␀Rª␀␀␀␀␀␀Õª␀␀␀␀␀␀=º␀␀␀␀␀␀Íº␀␀␀␀␀␀ıº␀␀␀␀␀␀°Ω␀␀␀␀␀␀'æ␀␀␀␀␀␀»æ␀␀␀␀␀␀%ø␀␀␀␀␀␀ñø␀␀␀␀␀␀Îø␀␀␀␀␀␀ﬁ¡␀␀␀␀␀␀Î¬␀␀␀␀␀␀J√␀␀␀␀␀␀‡ƒ␀␀␀␀␀␀7≈␀␀␀␀␀␀§∆␀␀␀␀␀␀«␀␀␀␀␀␀i«␀␀␀␀␀␀»␀␀␀␀␀␀Ü»␀␀␀␀␀␀‡»␀␀␀␀␀␀A…␀␀␀␀␀␀õ…␀␀␀␀␀␀ˇ…␀␀␀␀␀␀^ ␀␀␀␀␀␀mÀ␀␀␀␀␀␀∆À␀␀␀␀␀␀)Ã␀␀␀␀␀␀«Õ␀␀␀␀␀␀-Œ␀␀␀␀␀␀îŒ␀␀␀␀␀␀"œ␀␀␀␀␀␀û–␀␀␀␀␀␀˝–␀␀␀␀␀␀u—␀␀␀␀␀␀Ê—␀␀␀␀␀␀]“␀␀